<!--
  RC 2027 Field — Static MuJoCo model
  ABU Robocon 2027 "The Pursuit of Mustika Nantantara" — MuJoCo 3.x, verified with 3.14.0

  Contents : 39 mesh geoms / 15 materials / 10 building-spot sites / 1 light + 3 cameras
             single file, no <body> (static field; append your robots yourself)
  Frame    : metres, z up, origin = centre of the field (field is 11.1 m x 11.1 m)
             corner-origin convention: corner = centred + 5.5 (both axes)
  Meshes   : meshes/field/*.obj (ASCII paths, relative to this file)

  Load:
      import mujoco
      m = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_path("mujoco_field/field.xml")   # 39 geoms / 39 meshes / 10 sites
      d = mujoco.MjData(m); mujoco.mj_forward(m, d)

  Windows note: MuJoCo's C++ layer cannot fopen non-ASCII paths. Keep this folder on an
  ASCII path (e.g. C:\rc2027\), or pass an assets dict to from_xml_string().

  Geometry (verified):
      ground 11.1 x 11.1, L1 6 x 6 x 0.6, L2 3 x 3 x 0.9, fences, both transition bands
      (stairs 3 x 300 + 1000 x 1000 transfer platform + 3500 ramp @ 9.74 deg), pillars,
      10 building spots (500 x 500, site list), 12 sky blocks + Mustika + storage zones.

  Collision: the mesh geoms are visual *and* collide via their convex hulls. That is fine
      for a static reference, but a convex hull of e.g. the perimeter fence fills the whole
      field — for simulation use field_with_objects.xml, which splits visual meshes from a
      primitive collision layer (see README).

  See README.md for the full spec, the movable-object variant, limitations and license.
-->
